    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n8028" root="حسن" body-key="H">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَحْسَنَةٌ</span></b>  [<i>A cause of good:</i> pl., app., ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَحَاسِنُ</span></b> ;
like as <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَسَاوٍ</span>, originally <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَسَاوِئُ</span>, is said to be pl.
of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَسَآءَةٌ</span>, originally <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَسْوَأَةٌ</span>]. You say, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هٰذَا الطَّعَامُ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَحْسَنَةٌ لِلْجِسْمِ</span> [<i>This food is a cause of good,</i>
i. e. <i>beneficial, to the body</i>]. (S.)

